 @AJDOLDCHANNELARCHIVE  No offense, but this drama around VRAM at 4k is totally pointless. Looking at MSRP you´re paying (probably) 300$ more for a 3080 TI instead of a 3080 for what? ~6-10GB more VRAM and,  if its between the 3080 and 3090 around 5-7% more performance, which translate to around ~5FPS in 4k in most games. That is terrible value, because no games goes from unplayable to playable with this performance difference. If you research that most new games reserve around 10Gigs of Vram, but actually use more like 7-8GB. No game next year will crash or not start in 4k. 
And lastly: Neither the 3080, 3080 TI or 3090 can play next-gen titles at 4k 144hz. So overspending now to "futureproof" in any kind is a terrible idea, like when people bought 2080 TI only to realize with the RTX 3000 how much money they wasted.
The only usefull recommandation at 4k is: Buy a 3080 now, sell it when the 4080 releases and do an upgrade, that card will have more VRAM if its needed at that time.

